{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/36891-annoyingly-stupid-questions-about-hisil","id":36891,"title":"Annoyingly stupid questions about Hisil.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-25T06:09:48-08:00","id":36891,"title":"Annoyingly stupid questions about Hisil.","content":"I'm doing a research for my mage chronicle, and i'm curious is there something like Middle Umbra, Deep Umbra or Penumbra in the nWoD. I also remember overhearing something about shortcuts in it, eg. Luna's Bridge. Can you tell me how wrong i am?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T07:52:20-08:00","id":36918,"title":"","content":"You can think of the state of Twilight as the analogue to the Penumbra, and the Shadow as the analogue to the Middle Umbra, roughly. Twilight isn't, properly speaking, a place; it's a state of matter, the state of being immaterial within the material realm, whereas the Shadow is the otherworld, reflecting the totemic truth of the world as it is rather than completely mapping its geography. War Against the Pure introduces lunar roads, which connect loci across the Shadow and are created by a rite reserved for Uratha warbands called to war by the lunes. The Shadow also occasionally contains places that do not correspond to anywhere in the physical world; given that, it's not inconceivable that there may be some naturally-occurring paths through it, though they may lead through strange and foreign territory.<br /> <br /> While not connected to Forsaken, if you're running Mage, the Temenos and Anima Mundi of the Astral Realms can be thought of as an analogue to the Deep Umbra in certain fashions, reflecting deeper and wider ideas and being much less literally connected to the shape of the physical world. Changelings have the Hedge, a midway between this world and Arcadia, and trods, which are paths which can be tread through the Hedge to get from one place to another distant place in this world quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T07:54:47-08:00","id":36921,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/36891-annoyingly-stupid-questions-about-hisil#post36891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm doing a research for my mage chronicle, and i'm curious is there something like Middle Umbra, Deep Umbra or Penumbra in the nWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral Realms, the Shadow, the Underworld, and the Hedge are all more or less separate otherworlds in the nWoD cosmology. The spirit world of the Shadow in itself is much like the old Penumbra, only darker and more vicious: for the most part, it corresponds roughly to the physical geography, with occasional anomalies in space and time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T08:48:18-08:00","id":36930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/36891-annoyingly-stupid-questions-about-hisil#post36891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm doing a research for my mage chronicle, and i'm curious is there something like Middle Umbra, Deep Umbra or Penumbra in the nWoD. I also remember overhearing something about shortcuts in it, eg. Luna's Bridge. Can you tell me how wrong i am?</div> </div> </div> </div>These terms belong to Werewolf: The Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T15:55:56-08:00","id":37048,"title":"","content":"There are &quot;far reaches&quot; in the Shadow. They're not easy to get to and have weird, ancient spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T17:04:46-08:00","id":37071,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for answers. It would take me a century looking it up in all those books...<br /> But to clarify:<br /> <br /> Twilight=Penumbra=?<br /> Shadow Realm=Middle Umbra=Hisil<br /> Deep Shadow?=Deep Umbra=Far Reaches?<br /> <br /> <br /> How those time and space anomaly's work? With space its pretty clear that the map looks just different in Hisil, but what with the time? You just happen to wander days, months, years, decades back in time? Can you use it as an time machine into real world or its just some memory?<br /> <br /> What are the werewolf suppose to do to travel through loci(over distance, not into shadow)?<br /> <br /> And what are those far reaches? Can you get there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T19:31:28-08:00","id":37108,"title":"","content":"Seriously, no. Guys, stop confusing the Moinen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T01:36:12-08:00","id":37230,"title":"","content":"Well. Now I'm really confused. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I know that umbras are from wta. I know how the mages view the Shadow Realm. I know that im mixing 3 gamelines WtA,MtA and WtF. I know. Chill. I said it there will be some stupid questions.<br /> Lets put it straight. How werewolves view it, and what interesting places or features of hisil they use? Shortcuts, weird places that are difficult to reach because the are deeper.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://willworks.deviantart.com/art/New-World-of-Darkness-Cosmology-Map-drawing-309999687\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://st.deviantart.net/minish/main/logo/default1200x630.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://willworks.deviantart.com/art/New-World-of-Darkness-Cosmology-Map-drawing-309999687\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found | DeviantArt </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://willworks.deviantart.com/art/New-World-of-Darkness-Cosmology-Map-drawing-309999687\" target=\"_blank\"> http://willworks.deviantart.com/art/New-World-of-Darkness-Cosmology-Map-drawing-309999687 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> DeviantArt is where art and community thrive. Explore over 650 million pieces of art while connecting to fellow artists and art enthusiasts. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-26-2013, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T03:32:39-08:00","id":37261,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/36891-annoyingly-stupid-questions-about-hisil?p=37071#post37071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How those time and space anomaly's work? With space its pretty clear that the map looks just different in Hisil, but what with the time? You just happen to wander days, months, years, decades back in time? Can you use it as an time machine into real world or its just some memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>The memories of how long journeys in the physical world have <i>felt</i> like may lead to distances in the Shadow shrinking or stretching out beyond the otherwise expected travel time. A particular highway might reflect the frustration of countless rush-hour commuters, for instance, so that getting anywhere along it proceeds at a snail's pace.<br /> <br /> &quot;Places That Aren't&quot; would be those that don't correspond to the material existence. For example, a skyscraper might have a thirteenth floor in the Shadow even though the building officially skips from 12 to 14.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}